== 6. Verdict against the pre-set criterion ==================== 
  PROMOTER-SPECIFIC = adjusted effect keeps >60% at p < 0.05 AND 
                      TSS-proximal probes in the extreme 5% of the null 
  GLOBAL CONFOUND   = keeps <60%, OR probes outside the 10% tail 
  PARTIAL           = in between; unresolved, NOT support 
 
  RASSF9: PROMOTER-SPECIFIC 
    unadjusted beta -1.352 -> fully adjusted -1.826 (135% retained, p = 6.95e-12) 
    TSS-proximal null percentiles: 0.81%, 0.12%, 0.00%, 0.00%, 0.29% 
 
  RASSF10: GLOBAL CONFOUND NOT EXCLUDED 
    unadjusted beta -1.029 -> fully adjusted -1.471 (143% retained, p = 3.31e-06) 
    TSS-proximal null percentiles: 18.74%, 23.77%, 47.89%, 0.46%, 0.06%, 2.26%, 3.53%, 0.93%, 1.45% 
 
  ASYMMETRY, stated so it cannot be read both ways later: the global 
  index is itself partly driven by purity, so adjusting for it also 
  removes real promoter signal. Surviving is therefore strong 
  evidence; not surviving is failure to EXCLUDE the confound, not 
  proof of one. 

